$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{8\\cdot {11}^{n}}{{9}^{n}} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{{11}^{n}}{{9}^{n}} \\\\  & =8{(\\frac{11}{9})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now see that this is the geometric sequence with $r=\\frac{11}{9}.$ \n\nSince $|r|>1,$ the sequence diverges." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "024681eacd50d272bc000914d0dae0ae76e6f051f0fce1d4415fcab82dd2bdfd"} {"question" "q-141314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Converges to $0$"] ["text" "Converges to $1$"] ["text" "Converges to $8$"] ["text" "Converges to $\\frac{11}{9}$"] ["text" "The sequence diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The sequence diverges"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-49565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Does the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{3{(2)}^{n}}{{5}^{n}}$ for $n\\ge 1$ converge or diverge? If it converges, what is its limit?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-49565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{3{(2)}^{n}}{{5}^{n}} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{n}}{{5}^{n}} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{5})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now see that this is the geometric sequence with $r=\\frac{2}{5}.$ \n\nSince $|r|<1,$ the sequence converges to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-49565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "024681eacd50d272bc000914d0dae0ae76e6f051f0fce1d4415fcab82dd2bdfd"} {"question" "q-49565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" 