-\\frac{4}{6})}^{n} \\\\  & =3{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now see that this is the geometric sequence with $r=-\\frac{2}{3}.$ \n\nSince $|r|<1,$ the sequence converges to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "024681eacd50d272bc000914d0dae0ae76e6f051f0fce1d4415fcab82dd2bdfd"} {"question" "q-141310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Converges to $-\\frac{2}{3}$"] ["text" "Converges to $0$"] ["text" "Converges to $3$"] ["text" "Converges to $\\frac{2}{3}$"] ["text" "The sequence diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Converges to $0$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Does the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{4{(-7)}^{n}}{{2}^{n}}$ for $n\\ge 1$ converge or diverge? If it converges, what is its limit?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nFirst, we rewrite the sequence in the form ${a}_{n}=a\\cdot {r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{4{(-7)}^{n}}{{2}^{n}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{(-7)}^{n}}{{2}^{n}} \\\\  & =4{(-\\frac{7}{2})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now see that this is the geometric sequence with $r=-\\frac{7}{2}.$ \n\nSince $|r|>1,$ the sequence diverges." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "024681eacd50d272bc000914d0dae0ae76e6f051f0fce1d4415fcab82dd2bdfd"} {"question" "q-141312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Converges to $-\\frac{7}{2}$"] ["text" "Converges to $0$"] ["text" "Converges to $4$"] ["text" "Converges to $\\frac{7}{2}$"] ["text" "The sequence diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The sequence diverges"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-351615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the geometric sequence ${a}_{n}=12{(\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ Find the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges.\n\n$x$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-351615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}.$ \nSince ${x}^{2}$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}\\ge 4.\n$$\n\nTaking into account the fact that $x$ is positive, we get\n\n$$\nx\\ge 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-351615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "024681eacd50d272bc000914d0dae0ae76e6f051f0fce1d4415fcab82dd2bdfd"} {"question" "q-351615" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-351615" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-351615" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-351615" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the geometric sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{x}{4}{(\\frac{8}{x})}^{n},$ where $x$ is a positive real number and $n\\ge 1.$ What are the values of $x$ for which the sequence converges?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r=\\frac{8}{x}.$ \nSince $x$ is positive,  $r$ is also positive, So, the convergence condition is $0<r\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, the  sequence converges for \n\n$$\n0<\\frac{8}{x}\\le 1\\,⟹\\,x\\ge 8.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e394b0498f7c0cd247c708f1eb97231f17f2a2ac880e99ea31c626105221cc1"} {"question" "q-141323" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "024681eacd50d272bc000914d0dae0ae76e6f051f0fce1d4415fcab82dd2bdfd"} {"question" "q-141323" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031858